{"text": "PHILIP MORRIS U.S. A\nC89-02181\nINTER-OFFICE CORRESPONDENCE\n\nRichmond, Virginia\n\n0 H. Alonso . Date: April 11, 1989\nRESTRICTED\nFrom: wR. G. URL DISTRIBUTION (307\nSubject: .RECONSTITUTED TOBACCO DEVELOPMENT--WEEK OF APRIL. 9, 1989}\n\nRL_PILOT PLANT\n\nCommenced replacement of the RBM, SBM, and Mix tanks; installation and\ncheckout continues through the week of 4/10.\nant,\nCompleted the production of pilot RL sheets incorporating txipotassium\ncitrate cased CRS (half utilization level): these and the sheets containing\nmonopotassium citrate cased CRS will be evaluated against ART stem RL in\nhandmade 1008 cigarettes prior to requesting blends. Neutralizing ART stems\nmay not be beneficial; 150B (size ph 6.7) smokes worse than TC (size ph\n5.3). Further base treatment (RCB slurry at ph 9.0) appears to help\n\nRCB with 22% ART stems is giving detectable mouthcoating in blends; the RCB\nincorporating 118 ART stems appears viable. The limit in RL is one-eighth\nutilization (1.8% of feedstock); although the 7C smokes better, doubling the\nART stem level puts it over the edge. The three sheets will be combined in\nsmall scale blends (total 30% utilization); other blend combinations are\nunder consideration. There is growing support for a subsequent Stockton\nSt. trial; pilot (or Park 500) production of the RL will be required.\n\nAlthough bottom basket stems smoke better than top basket, it has not been\ndetermined whether the bottoms are better than total stems or the tops are\nworse. Total stems post-treated in the Hauni HT tunnel smoke better than\nbottom basket stems; they still do not pass as half utilization RL in\nblends, but quarter utilization may be feasible. There are enough of the\nHauni stems to produce such sheet; this could also be tested using a mix of\nhalf utilization and control sheets (equivalency has not been established) .\n\n\u2018Three ART pilot runs (#332-4) had the top 5-6\" (<5% of total stems) removed\nfrom the top basket; the >95\u00a5 remaining stems were blended together \u2018for\nsheet making to determine if the subjective negatives of top basket stems\nare due to the wax layer settling out from the absorber headspace during\npressure letdown. In order to confirm this, scalping of the top basket was\n\ncontinued. New Tobacco Processes is drying the scalped material (-10 ibs 8\n/day) in the Sargent tray dryer; this will be conbined for sheet making (to 8\ndemonstrate a subjective negative) and extended chemical analyses. 8\nx\ncucanerme paren &\na\nContinued fabrication and sizing of handsheets with alternate fillers. oe\n7 2\nce: K. S. Burns D. B. Knudson c. HL Rowe A }\nBL G. Craze R. PL Lum 5. R. Wagoner es\nE. B. Fischer RL BL Merritt G. L. Wilkinson\nG. Gettatiy R. Prasad Konczal File\ns\n\nD. Keritsis", "words": [{"text": "PHILIP", "x0": 311, "y0": 67, "x1": 352, "y1": 74, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "MORRIS", "x0": 360, "y0": 67, "x1": 403, "y1": 75, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "U.S.", "x0": 418, "y0": 67, "x1": 445, "y1": 75, "conf": 24.0}, {"text": "A", "x0": 461, "y0": 68, "x1": 467, "y1": 75, "conf": 77.0}, {"text": "C89-02181", "x0": 44, "y0": 69, "x1": 124, "y1": 85, "conf": 71.0}, {"text": "INTER-OFFICE", "x0": 196, "y0": 95, "x1": 360, "y1": 103, "conf": 90.0}, {"text": "CORRESPONDENCE", "x0": 396, "y0": 95, "x1": 589, "y1": 104, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Richmond,", "x0": 332, "y0": 123, "x1": 393, "y1": 133, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Virginia", "x0": 404, "y0": 123, "x1": 460, "y1": 134, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "0", "x0": 110, "y0": 180, "x1": 123, "y1": 187, "conf": 31.0}, {"text": "H.", "x0": 182, "y0": 180, "x1": 188, "y1": 187, "conf": 61.0}, {"text": "Alonso", "x0": 203, "y0": 179, "x1": 245, "y1": 188, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": ".", "x0": 314, "y0": 189, "x1": 317, "y1": 190, "conf": 0.0}, {"text": "Date:", "x0": 461, "y0": 181, "x1": 488, "y1": 189, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "April", "x0": 511, "y0": 180, "x1": 546, "y1": 191, "conf": 54.0}, {"text": "11,", "x0": 556, "y0":